    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Automatically converts your JPEG and PNG uploads into Google’s WebP format. This plugin reduces image file sizes by up to 80% without sacrificing visual quality.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the <code>simple-webp-optimizer</code> folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Go to <strong>Settings -&gt; WebP Optimizer</strong> to configure.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>2.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial public release with bulk optimization support.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Auto-convert JPG/PNG to WebP. Save up to 80% server space and boost site speed with built-in bulk optimization and real-time savings reports.",
    "description": "<p>Automatically converts your JPEG and PNG uploads into Google’s WebP format. This plugin reduces image file sizes by up to 80% without sacrificing visual quality.</p>\n",
